WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.089
Make no mistake: Mowgli: Legend of the Jungle
may be based on The Jungle Book, but it's

00:00:05.089 --> 00:00:06.760
definitely not for children.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:11.620
When Andy Serkis announced his plans to direct
a live-action adaptation of The Jungle Book,

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:12.920
no one batted an eyelash.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:18.520
Disney's 1967 animated original was an instant
classic, with wholesome elements that viewers

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:22.580
of all ages could enjoy, folded into a story
of self-discovery.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:25.740
Wouldn't Serkis' adaptation be just as delightful?

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.480
Unfortunately, things panned out poorly for
Mowgli.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.520
Not only did it bomb with critics when it
launched in a limited theatrical run at the

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:37.220
end of November, it also went over terribly
with a certain subset of its audience when

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.020
it hit Netflix on December 7th, 2018.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:45.740
Parents discovered that, not too unexpectedly
given the films' PG-13 rating, Mowgli is riddled

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:50.730
with violence against humans and animals,
soaked with bloodshed, and features a horrifying

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:53.560
death that is continually referenced throughout
the narrative.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:58.739
Those parents and guardians have come forward
to let others know that Mowgli is, quote,

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:01.940
"traumatizing," and that they shouldn't let
their kids watch a second of it.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:04.280
One viewer wrote on Twitter, in part,

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.060
"#Mowgli what…the…f---???"

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.520
"That twist is some sadistic s---.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.680
I mean, kids would be traumatized."

00:01:10.689 --> 00:01:11.740
Another tweeted,

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:12.240
"Dang.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.580
This #Mowgli adaptation on Netflix is not
really a kid's movie.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:17.940
It's got some harsh scenes."

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:22.600
One parent alerted others of a particular
scene's potentially psychologically damaging

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:23.600
effects, saying,

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.660
"There is a scene in #Mowgli that will absolutely
scar and shock young kids.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:29.680
Parents be warned.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.520
This version is incredible but VERY dark."

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:37.240
Plenty more on social media have warned that
Mowgli is "not for kids" and will take you

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:41.459
by surprise with how dark it is, and that
if they were a child watching Mowgli, they

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:44.660
would be forever haunted by a certain character's
creepy eyes.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.390
It seems that many parents, likely rundown
in chasing after their children all day or

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:53.509
clocking in eight hours at the office that
day, figured that Mowgli would be appropriate

00:01:53.509 --> 00:01:58.340
for the whole family and immediately pressed
"play" on Netflix without a second thought.

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:02.920
Sadly, they unknowingly bit off far more than
they or their kiddos could chew.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:06.700
While parents have been warning others to
steer clear of Mowgli when their kids are

00:02:06.709 --> 00:02:11.099
around now that the film is on Netflix, critics
were doing exactly that when the film was

00:02:11.099 --> 00:02:12.120
still in theaters.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.820
A review on Decider warned,

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:18.720
"The action scenes where Mowgli is in danger
are legitimately scary, and probably traumatic

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.320
for very little kids, so buyer beware.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:25.319
Definitely think it over before traumatizing
your kids with it […] Unless you're a giant

00:02:25.319 --> 00:02:29.519
Jungle Book aficionado and crave completism,
you can Skip It."

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:33.300
The Independent called it, quote, "relentlessly,
discordantly bleak.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.980
[…] Not quite a kid's film, not quite an
adult's one."

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:40.819
Just two years ago, Jon Favreau released his
Walt Disney Pictures-produced Jungle Book

00:02:40.819 --> 00:02:43.909
to critical acclaim and immense box office
success.

00:02:43.909 --> 00:02:46.540
"Relax, kid, no need to get worked up, kay?"

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:47.740
"Where am I?"

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.680
"Uh, this is a cave.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:51.640
It's my cave."

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.870
The pic scored an Academy Award for Best Visual
Effects, smashed records to become one of

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:02.220
the top-grossing movies of 2016, and Rotten
Tomatoes summarized the film's reviews with,

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:06.840
"[Jungle Book is] the rare remake that actually
improves upon its predecessors, all while

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.670
setting a new standard for CGI."

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:13.420
It would be impossible for Serkis to replicate
the magic of Favreau's film, but it was hardly

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:17.489
a stretch to assume that Mowgli could pick
up praise from members of the media and make

00:03:17.489 --> 00:03:19.720
Disney fans young and old smile.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:24.819
Sadly, while a handful of reviewers have respected
Serkis' grim approach to The Jungle Book,

00:03:24.819 --> 00:03:29.340
the general consensus is that the director
went off the deep end and made things entirely

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:30.080
too dark.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:34.940
His desire to create something different with
Mowgli was, ultimately and unfortunately,

00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:35.510
his undoing.

